# Cache policy for Workers Static Assets.
#
# Workers Assets ships exactly one default for every file it serves:
#
#   Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
#
# That is the right answer for HTML — a deploy lands immediately, and a crawler
# revalidating on each fetch is what keeps the prerendered pages fresh in the
# index — so HTML is deliberately left on it and is not listed here.
#
# It is the wrong answer for /assets/*. Everything Vite emits there is
# content-addressed: the hash in the filename IS the cache key, and a changed
# file arrives under a new name. Revalidating those costs a conditional round
# trip per asset on every repeat visit and can never return anything but 304.
# The service worker's cacheFirst rule hides this for returning visitors, but
# only after it has registered — never on a first visit, and never for a
# crawler, which does not run service workers at all.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
